# WHITELIST: track nothing unless it is allowed below.
#
# The source tree this release is cut from mixes code with UK Biobank-derived data, including exact
# private counts and individual-level (k = 1) item files. With a blacklist, one missed rule puts a
# private file into git history, where it cannot be taken back once pushed. Here a new file has to be
# allowed in explicitly, and tools/check_release.py runs over everything that is allowed before any
# commit or push.
*
!.gitignore
!*/

# ---- top level ----
!README.md
!LICENSE
!CITATION.cff
!requirements-freeze.txt

# ---- environment packages (deliverable 3) ----
!cohortworld_env/**
!cohortworld_internal/**
!cohortworld_locate/**
!cohortworld_delta/**
!cohortworld_phenocal/**

# ---- prompts and eval configs ----
!prompts/**
!configs/**

# ---- scoring and reproduction (deliverables 4 and 6) ----
!gen/**
!reproduce/**

# ---- cohort-collection build scripts, for provenance (deliverable 1; need UKB access to run) ----
!build/**

# ---- training (deliverable 5) ----
!train/**

# ---- tests, release tooling, data manifests (no data) ----
!tests/**
!tools/**
!data/README.md
!data/MANIFEST.tsv

# ---- website screenshots, shown in place of the live URL while review is double-blind ----
!docs/site/*.png

# ---- never, even inside an allowed directory (last matching rule wins) ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
**/priv/
**/*private*
**/*_subject*
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.idx
*.npz
*.parquet
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.log
outputs/
experiments/
